{"namespace":"uhm","outcome":"answer","exit_code":0,"executed":false,"message":"`git log --oneline` shows the commit history in a compact format: one commit per line.\n\nEach line contains:\n- an abbreviated commit hash\n- the commit’s subject (first line of its message)\n\nExample:\n```text\n3fa12bc Fix CSV parsing for quoted fields\n91d7e20 Add sales import command\n4be8a6f Initial project setup\n```\n\nIt is equivalent to `git log --pretty=oneline --abbrev-commit`."}
